From 08880683058e2c4e32dd0c0c48ef5774ed1cb123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 18:03:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/25] Judge a quiet search by its own pace, and stop
 colouring container logs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The watchdog compared every search against its busiest neighbour on the
same site: if "waterproof jacket" kept finding listings, "Rab Downpour"
going quiet for a hundred minutes was "stale". But the niche search sees a
listing a week and returns four results on a page that holds ninety-six.
Now a search whose last page was not full is never called stale — a frozen
feed serves the same full page forever, a niche search serves what little
there is — and a full-page search has to be quiet for six times its own
median gap between listings (from the listing times already recorded), and
two hours at least, before it counts. Migration 0009 records the last page
size.

Console logs used ANSI colours whenever stderr was a TTY, which a container
started with one reports even when the reader is Portainer's log viewer;
it renders the escape codes as a smear of repeated words. Colours are now
off unless LOG_COLOR=true.
